guide forever/miscellaneous/cozy-sleeping-bag
title Cozy Sleeping Bag
category Miscellaneous
keywords Cozy Sleeping Bag, Old Toolbox, Student Fodder, ... and that note you found, Stepping Stones, Scramble, Wet Job, Eagle's Fist, This Must Be The Place, Burned-Out Remains, Nailed Plank, Thoradin's Wall
collects 211527, 221498
reward item 211527
reward item 221498
why A trail of hidden notes across both continents: the Cozy Sleeping Bag at the end, a 12-slot Old Toolbox on the way.
levels 14-32
zone Westfall

# The six-quest chain Forever kept from Season of Discovery, at lower levels
# (22-32, needs 14). Every quest starts and ends at a game object; none has
# objectives, so each step is a hand-in at the next hiding place.
# Every quest of the chain needs level 14 (minLevel in data/forever), so each
# faction's first step waits for it with `level 14` before the player sets
# out; Polestar starts only Class guides at their gate by itself (#698).
# Sources:
# - Quests, objects and their spawns: data/forever (QuestieDB Forever):
#   79008 / 79007 ... and that note you found, 79192 Stepping Stones, 79980
#   Scramble, 79974 Wet Job, 79975 Eagle's Fist, 79976 This Must Be The Place.
# - The order per faction: 79008 (Alliance) starts at the Westfall remains
#   (415107) and ends at the Barrens ones (415106, Nailed Plank 417072); 79007
#   (Horde) the reverse (Westfall Nailed Plank 424010). Stepping Stones starts
#   at either plank.
# - Rewards (Old Toolbox 221498 from Stepping Stones; Cozy Sleeping Bag 211527
#   and Student Fodder from This Must Be The Place), the path into the
#   Stonetalon hills (about 50.9,52.3) and the climb to the Messenger Bag from
#   the Hillsbrad side of Thoradin's Wall (a fallen cart against the wall, about
#   87.5,47.7 in Hillsbrad Foothills): Forever's quest data and players'
#   reports, from the local archive, facts only.
# - Alliance come into Stonetalon from the north (#1813): the Barrens' way in
#   runs through Honor's Stand (about 39.4,29.7, map 1413), a Horde post, and
#   on to the hills it passes Malaka'jin and Sun Rock Retreat. Players'
#   recordings of Stepping Stones (Alliance): about 40 runs, most entering from
#   the Barrens (Stonetalon 83.5,97), 7 people dead at Honor's Stand and one in
#   Sun Rock; the runs by the Talondeep Path (Ashenvale 42.4,71.0 to Stonetalon
#   81.6,30.1) and off the Stonetalon Peak flight lost nobody there.
# - The way off the dam: players' recordings (2026-11-09 pull). From the
#   ledge most players drop into the river below the dam (Wetlands); 22
#   contributors died at its waterfall, about 65.0,77.4 and 66.7,75.1 (map
#   1437), while those who left it on the west bank (about 67,81 to 61,73)
#   lived and took the road north over Thandol Span. The Thoradin's Wall
#   step's two gotos follow the survivors' tracks out of the river (64.4,79.4
#   then 62.2,76.8); those who died turned back north-east into the river at
#   the first of them.
# Not play-tested on Forever yet.

step The note in Westfall
  only Alliance
  tip The chain opens at level 14. A burned-out campfire in western Westfall, with a nailed plank beside it.
  level 14
  accept 79008

step Its twin in the Barrens
  only Alliance
  zone The Barrens
  tip The note's "twin land" is the Barrens: the same burned-out campfire stands in the southern Barrens.
  turnin 79008
  accept 79192 object 417072

step The note in the Barrens
  only Horde
  zone The Barrens
  tip The chain opens at level 14. A burned-out campfire in the southern Barrens, with a nailed plank beside it.
  level 14
  accept 79007

step Its twin in Westfall
  only Horde
  zone Westfall
  tip The note's "twin land" is Westfall: the same burned-out campfire stands in western Westfall.
  turnin 79007
  accept 79192 object 424010

# Only for an Alliance player who is not yet in Stonetalon: once there (by the Talondeep Path or the Stonetalon
# Peak flight) the step drops (#1496, #1813).
step Stonetalon from the north
  only Alliance
  zone Ashenvale
  when !zone "Stonetalon Mountains"
  tip The Barrens' way into Stonetalon runs through Honor's Stand, and the road on to the hills passes Malaka'jin and Sun Rock Retreat: all Horde posts. Come in from the north instead. With the Stonetalon Peak flight path, fly there and follow the road south. Otherwise fly to Astranaar and walk south-west to the Talondeep Path, the tunnel from Ashenvale into Stonetalon.
  goto 42.4,71.0 map 1440 "The Talondeep Path" r 25

step Stonetalon Mountains
  zone Stonetalon Mountains
  tip The next hideout is a small camp in the hills north-west of Sun Rock Retreat, in the middle of the Stonetalon Mountains. Leave the road where a path climbs west into the hills and follow it to the camp; the Pocket Litter lies on a crate beside its tent.
  goto 50.9,52.3 "Path into the hills"
  turnin 79192
  accept 79980

step A hundred paces north
  tip Walk north through the camp and drop carefully down the steep slope to the Mound of Dirt on the ledge below. A missed jump only slides you down: hug the cliff and walk back up.
  turnin 79980
  accept 79974

step The dam in Loch Modan
  zone Loch Modan
  tip The figurine is on a ledge just below the top of the Stonewrought Dam, on its north face. Step off slowly; walking backwards keeps you from overshooting the ledge.
  turnin 79974
  accept 79975

step Out of the river
  zone Wetlands
  tip Careful: off the dam's ledge you land in the river below it, in the Wetlands. Climb out on its west bank well before the waterfall at about 65,77: the fall kills. Then head north-west to the road and follow it north over Thandol Span into Arathi.
  goto 64.4,79.4 map 1437 "West bank, before the waterfall" r 12
  goto 62.2,76.8 map 1437 "West bank" r 15

step Thoradin's Wall
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip At the gate in Thoradin's Wall between Arathi and Hillsbrad, turn north and follow the wall on the Hillsbrad side to a fallen cart leaning against it. Jump up the cart and its ladder onto the wall, then over the rocks to the hidden camp. Some characters cannot fit under the cargo netting at the camp; another race or a smaller form gets through.
  goto 87.5,47.7 "Fallen cart"

step The hidden camp
  zone Arathi Highlands
  turnin 79975
  accept 79976
  turnin 79976
